  "name": "Example: Calculating the Speed of a Particle Given Its Velocity",
  "problem": "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $\\mathbf{u}=(5\\mathbf{i} +2\\mathbf{j}) \\,\\textrm{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle.",
  "worked_solution": "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|5i+2j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nkilometers per hour.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
